Part 2: Mandatory Data Protection & Privacy Addendum

5. Baseline Privacy Standard (Stricter than Swiss FADP): Any deployment, hosting, or execution of this Work that processes personal data must enforce technical and organizational protections that exceed the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (FADP). Specifically, operators must enforce:
   - Zero-Knowledge & End-to-End Encryption: Personal data must be encrypted at rest and in transit using strong cryptographic standards, ensuring operators cannot access plaintext user data without explicit cryptographic keys held solely by the data subject.
   - Strict Data Minimization & Purpose Limitation: No personal data, telemetry, or metadata may be collected, logged, or retained beyond what is strictly necessary for the immediate execution of the user-requested function.
   - Prohibition on Unauthorized Data Brokering: Personal data processed by this Work shall never be sold, rented, monetized, or shared with third-party data brokers or advertising networks.

6. Local & Jurisdictional Compliance: In addition to Section 5, any entity deploying or operating this Work must fully comply with all applicable data protection and privacy laws in their current geographic zone, region, or country (including, where applicable, GDPR, CCPA/CPRA, local data residency mandates, and national privacy statutes). Where local law and Section 5 conflict, the stricter privacy protection shall apply to the maximum extent permitted by law.

